WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.080
D-Class Personnel are the cogs that keep the
machinery of the SCP Foundation running smoothly.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.590
Unfortunately, things are rarely very smooth
for the personnel themselves. There’s a

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:15.830
reason that common knowledge basically states
the D stands for “Disposable.” The lab

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:21.529
rats of the SCP Foundation, D-Class is a role
that no one in their right mind wants to play.

00:00:21.529 --> 00:00:25.720
But what if you didn’t have a choice?
What if, somehow, whether through a shift

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:31.050
in time and space, or being accused of a crime
you didn’t commit, you found yourself transported

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:36.700
to a cell at an SCP Foundation site? Once
there, you quickly realize how dire your situation

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:42.489
is. But there’s hope! Maybe. You overhear
your fellow inmates whispering about other

00:00:42.489 --> 00:00:47.600
prisoners who managed to escape. Could you
use your knowledge of the SCP Foundation to

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.670
find your way back to freedom?
We posed this scenario, and question, to the

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:56.609
amazing fans of SCP Explained, and you told
us about all of the ways you would try to

00:00:56.609 --> 00:01:03.850
escape from the SCP Foundation before your
inevitable termination - or worse, transmutation.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:09.340
So let’s get right to it and see who would
make it out, and who would wind up in SCP-682’s

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:12.790
stomach.
JustDrake said, “Well, considering I’ve

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:17.580
quite enjoyed the VR game SCP: Labrat, I’d
wait for a good containment breach, maybe

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.970
release a few extra SCPs that may be contained
with me, trust no voice i hear (Looking at

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:29.060
you, SCP-939) and just make for some type
of hole created, or maybe sewage drain? I've

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.580
never beaten the game truthfully but it’d
be an adventure”

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:36.800
Video games are the best way to prepare for
real life! Everyone knows that! That’s why

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:41.980
Resident Evil made me great at killing monsters,
Animal Crossing made me a world-class fisherman,

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:46.160
and The Sims prepared me for those days when
the door to my room is suddenly replaced with

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:51.250
a painting of a clown! Really though, that
sounds like a solid strategy. Use the chaos

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:56.381
of a containment breach as cover, play Robin
Hood to some friendly SCPs, don’t follow

00:01:56.381 --> 00:02:00.570
any voices, and see if you can Shawshank Redemption
your way to freedom.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:04.970
What have you got to lose? Well, maybe your
life, but you probably wouldn’t hold onto

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:10.979
that for long at the Foundation anyway.
unwind said, “E Z P Z Having a leg up is

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:15.730
an understatement in this situation, having
watched scp explained videos we have a great

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:21.680
understanding about the foundation and the
scps even more so than the site director themselves.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.879
Just claim to be an O5 Council member from
a parallel universe and when interrogated

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:30.510
drop some classified information only they
would know, you'd be such a valuable resource

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:35.909
they might even let you join their council.
Not only have you escaped D-class duties you've

00:02:35.909 --> 00:02:41.510
also gained high amounts of power.”
Easy peasy indeed, just make an incredibly

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:46.420
bold claim and expose yourself as a potential
security risk! There’s a slim chance this

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:51.609
might work, but there’s also a pretty substantial
chance that the real O5 council will intervene

00:02:51.609 --> 00:02:56.670
and decide to go ahead and terminate you,
just in case. At the very least, you’d likely

00:02:56.670 --> 00:03:01.379
be placed in permanent protective custody.
But hey, maybe they’ll put you in one of

00:03:01.379 --> 00:03:04.139
the comfy cells with a minibar and everything.

00:03:04.139 --> 00:03:10.569
GamingRevelation said, “If I was escaping
I would use an audio clip of 682 screaming/destroying

00:03:10.569 --> 00:03:16.040
things and play it when people or SCPs are
nearby. The sounds of 682 will scare people

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:21.319
away or make a good enough distraction for
any guard stupid enough to fight 682. I would

00:03:21.319 --> 00:03:25.799
also email the audio file to myself, that
way I can use the audio file on basically

00:03:25.799 --> 00:03:29.930
any device”
This is an interesting one! You’d need a

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:35.090
lot of factors to line up just right for this
one to work, from keeping your phone (or another

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:39.760
device) on your person in spite of being in
Foundation custody, to finding a WiFi signal

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:44.709
to access your email, to making sure that
your audio file plays loudly enough to be

00:03:44.709 --> 00:03:48.989
convincing. Not sure what they have planned
for the next update, but currently the iPhone

00:03:48.989 --> 00:03:52.959
doesn’t emit sounds at a volume loud enough
to break through walls.

00:03:52.959 --> 00:03:56.810
There is a chance that the sound would strike
enough fear into the hearts of experienced

00:03:56.810 --> 00:04:01.890
guards to throw them off for a while anyway!
Just make sure SCP-682 doesn’t find out

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:05.450
what you’re up to – it probably doesn’t
appreciate copycats.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:11.480
Endertitan Gamezzz said, “I have a pretty
simple but solid escape plan I think:

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:16.660
STEP 1: Find out what site I'm at, what kind
of SCPs are contained there, are they dangerous

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:21.910
or harmless, how often are there containment
breaches, how often do D-Class die? If the

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:27.010
site seems safe enough then I'll just spend
my days meeting harmless SCPs like 999.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:31.240
STEP 2: If the site is dangerous, then I need
to do everything in my power to make sure

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:36.120
I'm not cross-tested with a dangerous SCP,
if that means stabbing my eye out or cutting

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:41.290
off my leg I'll do it, I'll do anything short
of killing myself if it keeps me away from

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:47.391
the likes of 106 and 682.
STEP 3: Try and see if any of the SCPs could

00:04:47.391 --> 00:04:52.590
help me escape, for instance, if 738 is at
the site then I'll find a way to get crossed

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:57.860
tested with it, and then ask to be free from
the foundation and have all my criminal records

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:02.950
wiped, sure it'll cost me but hey, at least
I'll be free. Or I could find a Keter class

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:08.380
SCP and see if we could help each other break
out, it's a risky option but once again I'd

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:11.440
do everything in my power to stay away from
the lizard.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:16.670
STEP 4: If all else fails then I'm either
gonna have to wait for or cause a massive

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:21.751
containment breach, then I can escape in the
confusion (all that time playing SCP Secret

00:05:21.751 --> 00:05:27.120
Lab will come in handy) once again its a risky
option and I don't really like my odds but

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:32.450
I'll take my chances if I have too.
STEP 5: If I die (and let's be honest I most

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:37.391
likely will) then I only have two requests
for the foundation, one, that they actually

00:05:37.391 --> 00:05:45.000
decide which SCP 001 is the real SCP 001,
and two, that my tombstone read "SUBSCRIBE

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:49.500
TO SCP EXPLAINED BECAUSE THEY MAKE FUN AND
ENTERTAINING VIDEOS! also screw the lizard."”

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:55.560
First of all, this isn’t a simple plan by
any means. It’s not a Canadian rock band

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:59.180
formed in 1999,
and it’s actually got quite a lot of detail.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:05.030
You’ve thought long and hard about this!
And we appreciate that! One note though, making

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:10.810
a deal with SCP-738 might not just cost you.
A previous D-Class was offered freedom by

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:16.200
the entity, at the cost of his best friend’s
death. Even after he took that deal with the

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:20.250
devil, he was recaptured by the Foundation
a mere five hours later. You can decide for

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:25.100
yourself if that’s really worth it. But
hey, if you’re that desperate, then go right

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:28.500
ahead. At least you’ve prepared for the
very worst.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:33.160
The first of your posthumous requests will
likely be denied, if we’re being honest.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:37.740
And the second request is very sweet of you,
look I’m blushing! But also, we’d prefer

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:41.290
if you didn’t put a Foundation target on
our backs by pointing out how many of their

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:46.380
secrets we’re revealing. You’re right
about one thing though. Can’t stand that

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:48.920
lizard.
Juan Torres said, “We’re going to need,

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:54.100
a teddy bear, an aluminum coated box, a chair
and desk, an intact human nervous system,

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:57.660
a dart gun, and lawn mulch.”
Wait, don’t stop there! You’re just going

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:01.360
to give us a list of ingredients and not finish
the recipe? I already went out and bought

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:04.470
all the stuff, and the nervous system won’t
stay fresh forever!

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:09.930
Superhamster said, “Plug 079 into the wi-fi.
It could cause a breach big enough, so hide

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:15.000
during the breach and then escape the ruined
facility. Let me explain further - 682 and

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:22.030
079 bonded, and 682 is famous for containment
breaches. 682 is very hard to re-contain.

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:28.760
So, if you help 079, he'll help 682, which
will help you. Also, many other dangerous

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:34.260
SCPs will be breached.”
Now this is thinking big! Sure, you’ll be

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:38.710
exposing the entirety of the world wide web
to an aggressive, unpredictable, and downright

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:43.930
rude Artificial Intelligence, but you’ll
probably be able to escape back into the world.

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:48.180
Who knows how much of the world will actually
be left after you’ve unleashed 079, 682,

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:54.740
and a whole host of other dangerous anomalies,
but the remaining rubble will be your oyster!

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:59.330
Creature Savage said, “Assuming I'm at a
site with an intelligent SCP that's known

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:04.990
for escapes, such as 682, I'd offer it a chance
at freedom if it helped me escape, and we'd

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:09.660
both take off for the infinite IKEA. Of course,
I could also offer Fernand the Cannibal my

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:15.110
services as a jester for his protection all
the way to and through the infinite IKEA”

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:21.020
Fernand the Cannibal! Now you’re talking!
If you manage to team up with that gargantuan

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:26.580
gentleman, he could definitely be a big help.
Just make sure he stays well-fed, or your

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:31.320
new friend is going to start wondering how
you taste with fava beans and a nice chianti.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:36.110
Otherwise, though, he’d love to have someone
listen to his stories and take the high part

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:41.089
during his favorite songs. Once you’re free
though, why not shoot for the stars? No need

00:08:41.089 --> 00:08:45.759
to fend off the murderous staff of the Infinite
Ikea, just go to a regular Ikea and get a

00:08:45.759 --> 00:08:49.129
new couch and some meatballs. No monsters
necessary.

00:08:49.129 --> 00:08:54.639
DelayAnimation said, “Before escaping, there
are multiple problems to overcome. You have

00:08:54.639 --> 00:08:59.490
to know the layout, Guards Patrol Paths, camera
placement, which Keycards you need, which

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:04.400
opportunities are best to escape. And once
you managed to find all of that out and escaped

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:09.550
to the outside you are still not done. Depending
on if you were in a Site or Area, the bare

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:13.800
wilderness surrounding a Site would be enough
to wreak havoc on you. Not to mention the

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:18.470
Watchtowers and outside Patrols. If you were
in an Area the Foundation would most likely

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:23.510
have Agents in the town surrounding the Area.
In conclusion, it is not possible to escape

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:28.420
the Foundations grasp. The only way to not
wind up as a Class D is to not do anything

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:32.589
to become a Class D.”
You know what they say, the best defense is

00:09:32.589 --> 00:09:38.040
a good offense! An ounce of prevention is
worth a pound of cure! However, there’s

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:42.209
not much offense or prevention you can do
when a temporal anomaly thrusts you into a

00:09:42.209 --> 00:09:46.900
parallel universe and plops you down right
in the middle of a D-Class cell. So, even

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:51.100
if you keep your hands clean your entire life
you might just find yourself in the custody

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:55.839
of the SCP Foundation anyway. It’s a nice
idea to think that just making all the right

00:09:55.839 --> 00:10:00.779
choices will prevent you from being falsely
imprisoned by a secret organization, but sadly

00:10:00.779 --> 00:10:04.490
life - and wormholes - just don’t work like
that.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:10.180
Zagham Shebaz Karim said, “The best thing
to do, is to make allies. First of all, you

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:14.839
need to get as many D-Class Personnel on your
side as possible. Ask them what duties they

00:10:14.839 --> 00:10:19.839
are on and use your information to help them.
Also, use them to find out what your duties

00:10:19.839 --> 00:10:24.959
are going to be as they will have connections.
You need to stay on the down-low, as if you

00:10:24.959 --> 00:10:29.290
are found out you will be experimented on
or worse. But, you don't only want to make

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:34.199
allies with the D-Class, armed with the knowledge
from SCP Explained you are able to guess/

00:10:34.199 --> 00:10:40.149
approximate which facility you are at, what
SCP's might be there, and who the staff are.

00:10:40.149 --> 00:10:44.589
With that knowledge, you can approach some
of the kinder staff and build your relationship,

00:10:44.589 --> 00:10:48.589
so in case you get caught when escaping you
have a fall back or someone that can bail

00:10:48.589 --> 00:10:53.240
you out of deadly punishments. You also want
to be resourceful and map out the place to

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:57.309
identify escape routes and the armory/ weapon
storage facility.

00:10:57.309 --> 00:11:02.149
Next, you want to form better relationships
with some of the SCP's. Before terminations

00:11:02.149 --> 00:11:06.840
roll around, you want to arrange a day that
the D-Class Personnel help some SCP's out

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:11.459
of containment. Mostly non-deadly ones as
you do not want to make an enemy out of the

00:11:11.459 --> 00:11:16.399
SCP Foundation. But enough to distract the
guarding personnel. Also, with your close

00:11:16.399 --> 00:11:20.950
contact with facility members, you have a
better chance at stealing credentials/ passes

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:25.680
to allow yourself through doors and escape.
But that isn't all, there actually might be

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:30.941
some SCP's on site that will make escaping
easier and your goal should not be just your

00:11:30.941 --> 00:11:36.259
own escape, but escaping with as many D-Class
Personnel as possible. You want to equip them

00:11:36.259 --> 00:11:41.500
with passes, all of them should know only
1 specific escape route which they themselves

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:46.190
or a few others are going, so that even if
they are caught, the others will not be found

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:51.209
out. And you want a few of them to escape
before everyone else and cause a ruckus outside,

00:11:51.209 --> 00:11:55.430
making it look like the whole group has escaped,
sending guards behind them.

00:11:55.430 --> 00:12:00.019
They will need access to a vehicle, so that
needs to be secured from one of the staff

00:12:00.019 --> 00:12:04.079
which could be captured during the escape
and used for a way out or you could steal

00:12:04.079 --> 00:12:09.290
their keys earlier, depending on the situation.
You yourself and a few others head to the

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:14.579
armory, to secure weapons, not only to escape
but to protect yourself from SCP's in the

00:12:14.579 --> 00:12:18.550
future. Then you need to secure vehicles for
the group, which you will need to put distance

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:23.209
between the facility and your group and stay
away from other nearby facilities.

00:12:23.209 --> 00:12:26.779
You need to stop at a certain point and go
to the nearest hospital to check for body

00:12:26.779 --> 00:12:32.459
implants or anything that can be used to track
you, changing clothes and continuing on by

00:12:32.459 --> 00:12:37.250
foot. At this point, your group can choose
to separate, live collectively, and stay alert

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:43.689
of the Foundation or join another organization”
This is probably the longest response we received,

00:12:43.689 --> 00:12:48.459
and we just had to include it to applaud the
dedication and thought at play here, as well

00:12:48.459 --> 00:12:53.029
as the selflessness! You’re not just planning
for your own rescue, no, that’s too small-time

00:12:53.029 --> 00:12:57.800
for Zagham. You’re planning to liberate
every D-Class you can, and potentially start

00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:01.720
your own brand-new society together. Make
sure you have a nice talk with them about

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:06.999
the rules for your new community, such as
“absolutely no stabbing your neighbors,”

00:13:06.999 --> 00:13:10.370
and enjoy all the great, trauma-free barbecues
that follow.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:14.639
Plot Armor said, “I would either attempt
to cause a containment break or steal an anomaly

00:13:14.639 --> 00:13:21.939
like SCP-268. Still, first I would draw thaumaturgic
symbols all over my body and clothes like

00:13:21.939 --> 00:13:27.050
Kalphastian isle which will make me resistant
to physical damage that will help me survive

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:30.709
containment breach.”
Bringing thaumatology into the equation is

00:13:30.709 --> 00:13:35.399
a brilliant move. You’d likely be the only
D-Class on site with any knowledge of that

00:13:35.399 --> 00:13:40.209
work, or the symbols. You’ll have to act
fast though, and work your magic before the

00:13:40.209 --> 00:13:43.329
Foundation figures out what you’re up to.
If you don’t, they’ll likely wipe your

00:13:43.329 --> 00:13:48.339
memory with amnestics or just terminate you
on the spot. The trickiest part of this plan

00:13:48.339 --> 00:13:53.390
is probably finding something to write with,
you can’t exactly ask to borrow a pen. But

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:58.880
between those and the hat, you could probably
slip out unnoticed and unscathed!

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:03.279
Jacob Oddie said, “I'd just do my best to
find Mr. Peanut so I could die relatively

00:14:03.279 --> 00:14:07.850
quickly/painlessly”
Why would that kill you? Are you allergic?

00:14:07.850 --> 00:14:12.819
…Just kidding, we know you’re talking
about SCP-173. As bleak of an answer as this

00:14:12.819 --> 00:14:17.569
is, we have to commend your honesty, and the
self-awareness it takes to look at the dangers

00:14:17.569 --> 00:14:23.439
of trying to escape the SCP Foundation and
simply saying: No, I’d rather not.

00:14:23.439 --> 00:14:27.129
Just another person On The Internet said,
“Well, taken with someone who has a very

00:14:27.129 --> 00:14:33.110
short attention span and who is a procrastinator
with ADHD, I could request a test with Miss

00:14:33.110 --> 00:14:37.949
J to see how it would affect someone like
me. Then I could escape and live the rest

00:14:37.949 --> 00:14:43.329
of my life in peace and solidarity.”
Miss J did help a previous D-Class leave the

00:14:43.329 --> 00:14:47.450
Foundation behind and start a new life, so
why not you too? We’re sure you’ll be

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:52.389
a model pupil, and wish you luck in whatever
discipline you decide to pursue! Don’t forget

00:14:52.389 --> 00:14:57.990
your number 2 pencil.
Milo Knight said, “SCP-6113 is a pretty

00:14:57.990 --> 00:15:02.569
surefire way to get out. Assuming you meet
the criteria you can suddenly have a different

00:15:02.569 --> 00:15:07.330
name and appearance, and you won't really
be on any Foundation records. Use that to

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:13.930
plead your case. Just pray you don't get terminated.”
This would be a pretty drastic choice, and

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:17.369
you’d probably have to double down on the
whole “new life” thing since none of your

00:15:17.369 --> 00:15:22.339
loved ones will recognize you - or you can
just tell them you got extreme reconstructive

00:15:22.339 --> 00:15:26.959
surgery, I guess. But it’s better to be
alive in a new body than dead in your usual

00:15:26.959 --> 00:15:31.470
one! As long as you’re able to avoid detection
following your transformation, and make sure

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:35.619
they don’t catch you on the security tapes,
this might just work.

00:15:35.619 --> 00:15:42.639
Zadanoire 0203 said, “I mean... you can’t.
Yes you’ll survive until the monthly “termination”

00:15:42.639 --> 00:15:46.940
but with how fortified these sites are, unless
you can get lucky with a containment breach

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:51.691
or are able to gain access to the sewer system,
you’re not escaping. and that’s not even

00:15:51.691 --> 00:15:56.280
taking into account your spontaneous being
here and having great knowledge on the foundation

00:15:56.280 --> 00:16:00.889
that you’d only really know if you were
a being above their perception. So on top

00:16:00.889 --> 00:16:05.400
of that, there’s also the potential of you
being terminated for knowing too much, or

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:09.550
being contained as a new scp.”
Hey now, we didn’t say “reply with the

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:13.550
best way to bum us out!”
Really though, we see all of you hyper-realistic

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:18.550
commenters and we get it, really! But in a
world filled with killer statues and friendly

00:16:18.550 --> 00:16:23.829
slime monsters, anything is possible. Sure,
most of the D-Class that wind up behind Foundation

00:16:23.829 --> 00:16:29.560
walls wind up dead, but you could be the one
in a million who makes it out. Dare to dream!

00:16:29.560 --> 00:16:35.019
Matt’s Magic said, “Easy, I simply say
"whoever shoots me or harms me is a rotten

00:16:35.019 --> 00:16:39.779
egg" and then walk out unharmed. Due to the
fact the guards are in fact people, not eggs”

00:16:39.779 --> 00:16:45.129
That’s it. You’ve cracked the code. Unless
the SCP Foundation starts hiring eggs as guards

00:16:45.129 --> 00:16:50.579
or creates some sort of unholy human-egg hybrid
to staff their halls - we’re looking at

00:16:50.579 --> 00:16:55.319
you, Humans, Refuted - their days of keeping
D-Class prisoners are over.

00:16:55.319 --> 00:16:59.430
